{title: 133 - Now Is Born the Divine Christ Child}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #133 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 133}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]He [Gm]was [F/A]born [Bb]in a [C7]stable [F]bare,
[F]On bed of straw how
[Gm]He sleeps so [C]soundly,
[F]He [Am/E]was [Dm]born [F/C]in a [C7/Bb]stable [F/A]bare,
[Dm]Let [C]us [F]worship and [Bb]to [C7]Him [F]bow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Ages long [Bb]since are [C7]past and [F]gone,
[F]When the wise men foretold His coming,
[F]Ages [Dm]long [F/C]since are [C7/Bb]past [Bb]and [F/A]gone,
[Dm]When the [C]wise [F]men foretold [C7]His [F]birth.
{end_of_verse}
